<Prose title="About ZipCostly" description="ZipCostly gives homeowners free, local cost estimates for home projects. No signup, no phone number, no sales calls." h1="About ZipCostly" needsReview>
  <p>ZipCostly answers one question: <strong>what will this project cost where I live?</strong></p>
  <p>
    Most cost guides give a single national average. But labor is often half the cost of a home project, and a plumber in Seattle earns very different money from one in Houston. We combine local wage data with current material prices to give you an itemized range for your ZIP code.
  </p>
  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No signup and no account.</li>
    <li>We never ask for your phone number or email, and we don't sell leads to contractors.</li>
    <li>We don't give one exact number, because real quotes vary. You always get a range.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How we make money</h2>
  <p>ZipCostly is free and supported by display ads. Ads never sit above or over your estimate.</p>
  <p>Want to know exactly how the numbers are built? Read our <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.</p>
</Prose>
